SUMMARY:Snuggles & Serenades w/Samara Jade
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\n**Please note that if you want to
  join us you must purchase a ticket- [reserve your spot HERE!!!](https://w
 ww.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/april-17th-snuggles-and-serenades-with-samara
 -jade)**\n\nJoin us for an evening of sweet connection and live music!\nWe
  will begin the evening with connection/intimacy-building exercises to fin
 d comfort\, open our hearts and set a clear container for connection befor
 e we settle into a sweet\, consensual\, safe cuddle space together. After 
 settling into connection\, our guest musician - **Samara Jade** will seren
 ade us with her original songs. Samara is a multi-instrumentalist\, and mu
 sical seamstress who threads together earthy grooves\, soul-soaked vocals\
 , and thought-provoking lyrics. **[Click here to check out Samara's music 
 & upcoming events!](https://www.samarajademusic.com/)**\n\nThe Cost for th
 is event is $20-45\, sliding scale\nSend us a message if you want to do wo
 rk trade.\n\nPlease arrive by 6:50 so that we can settle in\, connect\, & 
 create a sweet and safe container together before the music begins.\n\nThi
 s is a platonic touch based event that invites participants to explore con
 nection in a safe environment with like-minded people. We respect personal
  boundaries and through a supportive framework of mutual agreements that m
 aximize safety and create a space of easy openness and compassionate conne
 ction.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize touch and intimacy w
 ith clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-based touc
 h. We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun. We get our touch needs met.
 \nWe welcome people of all backgrounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, economic 
 statuses\, races\, spiritual or religious beliefs\, sizes\, and ages (18+)
 .\n\nTHE RULES\n1\\. Clothes stay on for the whole event\\.\n2\\. You do n
 ot have to touch anyone at this event\\.\n3\\. You must ask permission and
  receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone\\. Please be specific in you
 r requests\\.\n4\\. If you feel a yes\\\, say YES\\. If you feel a no\\\, 
 say NO\\. If you’re a maybe\\\, say NO\\. You can always change your min
 d\\.\n5\\. Get your facilitator if you have a question or concern\\\, or i
 f you need assistance with anything during the event\\.\n6\\. Talking\\\, 
 laughter\\\, silence\\\, silliness\\\, stillness\\\, and crying are welcom
 e\\.\nWHY CUDDLE?\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get
  enough\; most people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a
  way to ask for touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the pow
 er of touch\, and the importance of communication and consent in creating 
 a safe space for touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers 
 sounds weird or scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if som
 eone wants to touch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and 
 it’s not what I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and t
 hey say no?” These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is 
 a space created to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you
  don’t want. Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event. Most are r
 eally\, really glad they came.\n\nSchedule:\n6:45-7pm: Arrive with snacks 
 to share! Get comfortable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circ
 le- its mandatory. We will set our container\, talk about personal boundar
 ies\, communication\, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activ
 ities.\n8:00pm: Open cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ bef
 ore touching or cuddling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure h
 ow to do this – great! – we will talk about it during the welcome circ
 le.\n8:30ish Samara will begin to play music for us!!!\n10:50pm: Closing C
 ircle\, cleanup and head home.\nETIQUETTE\n\n* ARRIVE ON TIME: It is impor
 tant that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle. The Welcome C
 ircle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for consensual\, non-s
 exual touch between participants and making sure that everyone is informed
  about consent.\n* Please be free of strong scents\; many folks would rath
 er not be close to someone who smells of cigarettes\, perfume\, or essenti
 al oils. Your clean self is a good smell!\n* BE SOBER: Please do not drink
  or smoke before or at this event.\n\nWHAT TO BRING: personal water bottle
  and snacks to share\, a friend\, a date – whatever cuddle accessories y
 ou like! The only thing that you are required to bring is a clean and sobe
 r you.\nWe take individual and group safety seriously! if you experience\,
  see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be at a touch b
 ased event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to
  create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (ph
 ysical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm that
  takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know th
 at some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\nT
 hese events are not "gender balanced".\n\nWe take individual and group saf
 ety seriously! If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participa
 nts is not safe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are commi
 tted to doing our best to create a safe environment which means that if so
 meone is causing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here
  (this includes harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand beh
 ind survivors and know that some of our participants are here to heal from
  touch based trauma.\n\n\\*refund policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 days
  before the event.\nCredit towards a future event if you cancel more than 
 3 days before an event\, its due to an emergency\, or you are actively sic
 k.\nNo refund if you cancel the day before the event\, the day or no-show.
